Q: SharedPreferences Values not read within a flutter provider, or at least too late A: <p>You are calling <code>notifyListeners()</code> at the wrong place. The <code>notifyListeners()</code> is called before the async <code>initTest()</code> completes and hence the issue. Refer the following code for the fix:</p>
<h3>Minimal fix:</h3>
<pre class="lang-dart prettyprint-override"><code>
class SettingsProvider with ChangeNotifier {
  SettingsProvider() {
    initTest();
    // notifyListeners(); // Remove notifyListeners for here.
  }
  String? _currentAppUserId;

  void initTest() async {
    _currentAppUserId = await AsyncSharedPrefs.getString('currentAppUserId');
    // Uncomment the following to check the behavior when there's a delay:
    // await Future.delayed(const Duration(seconds: 3));
    print('currentAppUserId in initTest(): $_currentAppUserId');

    // Now tell the UI to refresh with the new value:
    notifyListeners();
  }

  String? get currentAppUserId {
    print('currentAppUserId in get currentAppUserId: $_currentAppUserId');
    return _currentAppUserId;
  }
}

</code></pre>
<p>When there's a delay in fetching the data, you will initially get a <code>null</code> value. You can choose to show a <code>CircularProgressIndicator()</code> when the retrieved value is <code>null</code>.</p>
<pre class="lang-dart prettyprint-override"><code>class MyHomePage extends StatelessWidget {
  const MyHomePage({super.key});

  @override
  Widget build(BuildContext context) {
    String? currentAppUserId = context
        .watch&lt;SettingsProvider&gt;()
        .currentAppUserId;

    if (currentAppUserId == null) {
      return const CircularProgressIndicator(); // Show a loader while waiting
    }

    print('currentAppUserId in _MyHomePageState: $currentAppUserId');
    return Text(currentAppUserId.toString());
  }
}
</code></pre>
